0,"last":2025,"intercept":16.642963508345943,"slope":-0.007834583186221029,"total":-0.7},"snow_normal":0.7},"titles":{"year":"2026 so far: 14 daily record highs, 3 daily record lows","records":"Waco is setting record highs far faster than chance","change":"Waco's nights cooled over the long run. Its days have warmed since 1986.","rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 73\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>73\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 70\u00b0F, and the record is 87\u00b0F (1951, 2005). The low of <strong>45\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Waco is setting record highs far faster than chance","p_rec":"If Waco's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Waco has set <strong>78 standing record lows</strong>, close to the 78 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">142 record highs</strong>, far more than the 78 that chance alone would give. The 2020s hold the most record highs of any decade (60). Waco's all-time high is 114\u00b0F, on July 23, 2018.","t_chg":"Waco's nights cooled over the long run. Its days have warmed since 1986.","p_chg":"Across 124 complete years: Waco's average low has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.11\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.18 to \u22120.04), about \u22121.3\u00b0F since 1902. Waco's average high shows no clear change: +0.08\u00b0F per decade, a range (0.00 to +0.16) that includes zero. It's close, but the range still includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows show no clear change and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.53\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.15 to +0.92). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; January fell. Highs rose in 3 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Waco's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.04 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 36.4 inches a year. The wettest year was 1905 (60.20 in); the driest, 1917 (13.39 in). Waco almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.7 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 14 daily record highs, 3 daily record lows"}}